title: $:/plugins/rimir/knowledge-app/changelog
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki

! Changelog

|!Version |!Date |!Changes |
|0.1.21 |2026-05-18 |Doc refresh to match 0.1.20's mindmap-driven shell. Rewrote `doc/architecture.tid` (new layers section: storage → resolution → app shell → navigation → preview; mindmap integration block describing producer args, node-filter operator, preview top-template, ns-backlinks wiring); `doc/reference.tid` (channels reduced to `area`/`note`; new filter chip state tiddlers; mindmap view tiddler fields; `kn-active-node-filter` operator; removed deleted-tab references); `doc/overview.tid` (features list rewritten around mindmap + chip filters + preview pane; prerequisites add mindmap); `doc/faq.tid` (added overlay-reset and tier-promotion entries; removed write-tab FAQ); `doc/examples.tid` (replaced "promote a note" with "filtering the mindmap" + "changing a note's type"; flagged source-render regression); `doc/dev-workflow.tid` (updated test list; replaced "Adding a new view" with "Adding a new note type" and "Adding a new mindmap producer arg"; flagged that the e2e spec needs rewriting). No behaviour change. |
|0.1.20 |2026-05-18 |''Folded the right-hand preview pane into the mindmap's built-in preview.'' (1) Removed the custom external preview pane from `apps/knowledge-main` — mindmap is now full width and uses its native preview (canvas 65% + preview 35%). (2) Wired the new `mm.preview-top-template` extension point (mindmap 0.2.29) to a small `templates/preview-top.tid` that transcludes the existing `kn-type-pill` interactive popup above the note body. The tier pill was dropped (no real value distinguishing this from the kn.type pill in the new context). (3) Set `mm.backlinks-filter` / `mm.outgoing-filter` on the mindmap view to use the namespace plugin's `ns-backlinks` / `ns-forwardlinks` (smarter than core operators because they follow context-resolution). Backlinks/outgoing now appear below the body in the mindmap's preview; clicking an entry re-selects the linked node in the canvas. (4) Bumped hard-dep `rimir/mindmap` requirement to ≥ 0.2.29. |
|0.1.19 |2026-05-18 |Mindmap-driven navigation. Replaced the left navigation tree with a `$mindmap` widget rendering the knowledge forest (all areas, area children collapsed initially). Selecting a node opens the existing note view as a preview pane to the right; with no selection the right pane is hidden and the mindmap takes full width. Tier and type filter chips above the mindmap multi-select and prune nodes with ancestor preservation. Dropped the `home`/`browse`/`write`/`search` sections from the app shell — the corresponding view files remain on disk as orphans for future re-introduction. New tiddlers: `apps/knowledge-main`, `views/knowledge-mindmap-view`, `procedures/filter-chips`, `filters/active-node-filter.js`. Layout switched to the new `topbar-main` layout (added to the appify plugin). Topbar simplified to area pills + `+ Note` + `+ Area`. Dependents now include `mindmap` (hard) and `mindmap-elixir` (soft). Requires `rimir/mindmap` ≥ 0.2.28 (new `knowledge-tree` producer args `collapse-below-depth`, `node-filter`, `node-filter-watch` and new `mindmap-title-for-op` filter operator). |
|0.1.18 |2026-05-18 |Dropped `type: text/plain` from the two shadow config tiddlers (`breadcrumb-max-entries`, `notes-tree-delimiter`). TW's filesystem adapter routes `text/plain` to extension `.txt`, which forces a split-file save (`<name>.txt` + sidecar `<name>.txt.meta`) whenever the user overrides via `<$edit-text>`. Default wikitext (no `type` field) keeps the override in a single `.tid` file. Consumers use `getTiddlerText` and don't read the type, so no behaviour change for the defaults. |
|0.1.17 |2026-05-17 |Test coverage push: 2 new `knowledge-has-broken-ref` specs — notes resolve via the `context` field (with no `\context` pragma) so detection matches render-time; mirror case ensures notes whose context-field resolutions all succeed are NOT flagged. Three `/* istanbul ignore */` annotations document defensive guards in `broken-refs.js` (empty-text, missing tiddler.text, REF_RE-guaranteed-capture). `broken-refs.js` now fully covered. Plugin coverage 60% → 63% lines; remaining gap is `focus-rewind.js` (DOM startup module — Tier D). |
|0.1.16 |2026-05-12 |Popup-edit modal: optional ''title-lock'' mode. When the state tiddler `$:/state/rimir/knowledge-app/popup-edit/title-lock` is set to `yes` before opening the modal, the modal renders with class `kn-popup-edit-title-locked`, hiding the EditTemplate's title row and dimming/disabling the title input. Save & Close and Cancel both clear the flag. Used by tw-mindmap when opening a note whose title was pre-derived from a node label slug — preventing renames that would break the slug ↔ tiddler mapping. Default behaviour unchanged when the flag isn't set. |
|0.1.15 |2026-05-06 |Descendant refs now resolve. From a deep note like `knowledge/llm/vendor/deepseek/model/v4`, writing `[[yt/AIsearch/engineeringDSV4]]` now resolves to `…/v4/yt/AIsearch/engineeringDSV4` automatically — no `\context` field needed. Implemented by enabling namespace's new ''self-prefix'' feature flag (namespace ≥ 0.1.13) via shadow `$:/config/rimir/namespace/self-prefix: yes`. Walk-up still handles the other direction (parent / ancestor refs) unchanged. Toggle the flag off in ControlPanel if you want strict resolution. |
|0.1.14 |2026-05-06 |Type-specific capture and render forms — opt-in extension surface for note types. The quick-capture modal now transcludes `forms/capture-<type>` (when present) below the type select; the Note view transcludes `forms/render-<type>` above the body. First implementation: ''source''. Capture form adds `caption`, `kn.author`, `kn.medium` (article/book/youtube/podcast/blog), `kn.url`, `kn.published` (with year/date granularity toggle), `kn.consume-status` (created/partial/consumed/reconsumed) and `kn.consume-date`. Render form shows a YouTube embed when the URL parses to a video ID (regex covers watch?v=, youtu.be, /embed/), with three player sizes (small default / medium / large) chosen via pill buttons under the player; per-note size lives in `$:/state/rimir/knowledge-app/source-yt-size/<noteTitle>`. Fields are displayed as a small definition list; each row has a hover-revealed pen icon to inline-edit just that field (text input / date / number / select per field type), exited with a ✓ button — per-note edit state at `$:/state/rimir/knowledge-app/source-edit/<noteTitle>`. New shadow tiddlers: `forms/source-helpers` (\\function `knowledge.yt-id`, `knowledge.medium-icon`, `knowledge.consume-icon`), `forms/capture-source`, `forms/render-source`. Quick-capture also resets all source-form state on Create. Tests: 11 specs covering yt-id parsing variants and icon mappings |
|0.1.13 |2026-05-05 |Card types: added two TZK types that were missing from the initial set — `conversation` (💬, raw notes from a meeting/discussion) and `note` (📝, raw notes from an ephemeral or non-print source like a lecture). Both join the existing `core` group alongside idea / source / sink. Type list grows from 13 → 15. Journal remains out of scope for the knowledge app (handled by priv-app). |
|0.1.12 |2026-05-04 |Sidebar Tiers section is now ''global''. The tier counts (3 fleeting, etc.) are computed across all areas, but clicking "🪶 Fleeting" used to keep the active area filter — so a user with 3 fleeting notes in `knowledge/inbox/…` and 0 in `knowledge/health/` would see the count "3" but an empty Browse. Now the tier buttons add `area=""` to their navigate target, clearing the area at the same time the section flips to Browse. Section header annotated with "(all areas)" to make this explicit. Browse header now shows a small diagnostic line with the live `area`, `prefix`, `tier` and `matches in source` count, useful for understanding what the view is computing |
|0.1.11 |2026-05-04 |Two related fixes for area browsing. (1) Browse no longer used `:filter[removeprefix[knowledge/]split[/]first[]match<activeArea>]` (which was unreliable in this rendering context); replaced with a pre-computed `areaPrefix` (`knowledge/<area>/`) and a direct `prefix<areaPrefix>` source filter. Same for the sidebar count and area-list. The active-area variable in the sidebar-area condition flow now propagates without a `:filter` subfilter and notes appear correctly. (2) The sidebar in area mode now lists ''actual notes'', not just first-segment topic names. Each entry is the note title with the `knowledge/<area>/` prefix stripped (e.g., `Crema`, `logo`); clicking it navigates to the Note view (`section=note, note=<full-title>`) and highlights the active note. The previous "sub-topics" view only listed segment names whose click set `topic=<seg>` but didn't open any note, leaving the main pane empty |
|0.1.10 |2026-05-04 |Fix: tiddlers created in earlier sessions (or by other means) under `knowledge/health/…`, `knowledge/llm/…` etc. weren't visible in Browse because the source filter required the `$:/tags/rimir/knowledge-app/note` tag — and tiddlers from before 0.1.8 (or hand-edited ones) lacked it. Switched the source filter from tag-based (`tag[$:/tags/rimir/knowledge-app/note]`) to ''title-prefix-based'' (`prefix[knowledge/]`). Any tiddler whose title starts with `knowledge/` is now treated as a knowledge note, regardless of how it was created. The capture/linkcatcher/inline-promote paths still set the tag (and `kn.tier`, `context`) for forward-compatibility and metadata, but visibility no longer depends on it. Tier filters and stats still depend on `kn.tier` — untagged legacy notes will show as missing from tier views; clicking ✎ Inline on them once promotes them automatically |
|0.1.9 |2026-05-04 |Fix: notes created in an area didn't show up in Browse / sidebar tree. Root cause: per `tw-statewrap-get-variable.md` the `\function` mechanism is unreliable inside appify-rendered views — `[function[knowledge.notes]] :filter[…]` and similar chains silently returned empty when the source filter relied on a `\function` call. The total-count selectors (`[function[knowledge.notes]kn.tier[fleeting]]` chained inside a single `[…]`) happened to work, masking the bug. Workaround per memory: inline the source filters in views. Replaced every `[function[knowledge.X]]` call across `views/*`, `apps/knowledge-{topbar,sidebar}.tid`, `procedures/{note-card,quick-capture-modal,popup-edit-modal}.tid` with the inline equivalent. The `\function` definitions in `filters/helpers.tid` are kept for the Jasmine tests, which run outside the appify rendering tree |
|0.1.8 |2026-05-04 |Notes created via in-body link click are now properly tagged. Previously: clicking `[[NewIdea]]` from a note in `knowledge/llm/…` navigated to `knowledge/llm/NewIdea` (good) but the eventual tiddler was created via inline-edit's `<$edit-text>` which only writes the `text` field — no `$:/tags/rimir/knowledge-app/note` tag, no `kn.tier`, no `context`. Result: the new note never appeared in Browse / Recent / Write. Fix is two-fold: (1) the linkcatcher pre-creates the target tiddler with the full note metadata when it's in the `knowledge/` namespace and doesn't yet exist; (2) the ✎ Inline button itself promotes any untagged `knowledge/…` tiddler to a proper note before entering edit mode (sets the tag, kn.tier=fleeting, and context derived from the title's area segment). Companion fix: statewrap 0.1.6 dedupes consecutive identical breadcrumb pushes so re-clicking the same link doesn't stack duplicates |
|0.1.7 |2026-05-04 |Area-aware capture and breadcrumb. (1) Quick-capture inside an area drops the `/inbox/` segment — typing `Foo` while LLM is active now creates `knowledge/llm/Foo` instead of `knowledge/llm/inbox/Foo`. The "no area" default still routes to `knowledge/inbox/`. (2) Clicking an unresolved `[[Foo]]` link inside a note also gets the area prefix: a new `knowledge.area-resolve(target,area)` filter helper returns `target` as-is when it already exists, is absolute (`knowledge/…` or `$:/…`), or no area is active — otherwise it prepends `knowledge/<area>/`. So `[[NewIdea]]` clicked from a note in `knowledge/llm/…` navigates to `knowledge/llm/NewIdea`, ready to be created. (3) Breadcrumb labels strip the active-area prefix for display via a new `knowledge.short-label(title,area)` helper — `knowledge/llm/Foo` shows as `Foo` while LLM is active, full path elsewhere. Applied to linkcatcher navigation, note-card clicks, and post-capture navigation |
|0.1.6 |2026-04-30 |In-body link navigation. Clicking a `[[xyz]]` link in the rendered note body now switches the Note view to that target instead of trying to push it onto the (non-existent) story river. Implemented by wrapping the body in `<$linkcatcher>`, whose `actions` fire `<$action-statewrap-navigate label=<<navigateTo>> section="note" note=<<navigateTo>>/>`. Each navigate pushes onto the app's nav-history stack — the topbar now also transcludes `$:/plugins/rimir/appify/ui/nav-breadcrumb`, so the breadcrumb shows the trail. Section + area pills clear the history on click (per `appify-navigation` convention). Click `<` segments in the breadcrumb to walk back; `$action-statewrap-back` restores the channel snapshot |
|0.1.5 |2026-04-30 |Delete a note from the Note view. New 🗑 button in the action bar; first click switches to a "Delete? [Yes] [No]" confirmation; Yes deletes the tiddler, clears the `note` channel, and switches back to Browse. State is per-note (`$:/state/rimir/knowledge-app/delete/<noteTitle>`) so a stray confirmation doesn't carry over between notes. (Companion fix in appify 0.2.27 makes EvidentlyCube/AutoComplete popups appear inside appify apps, including knowledge.) |
|0.1.4 |2026-04-30 |Cleaner edit experience. (1) Inline edit textarea is now full-width and ~480 px tall (CSS targets `.kn-inline-edit-wrap textarea.tc-edit-texteditor`, mirroring priv-app's journal editor). (2) The `\context` pragma is no longer prepended to new note bodies — the namespace context is stored as a `context:` field instead, kept invisible to the editor. Enabled the `implicit-context` namespace feature flag so the resolver picks up the field. Body of new notes is now pure user content. Existing notes that already have `\context` in body keep working (pragma takes precedence over field) |
|0.1.3 |2026-04-30 |Edit-mode polish. Reuses the theme plugin's shared editor templates (`rr-text-view-editable` + `rr-text-editor`) instead of a custom `<$edit-text>`, so notes get: ''double-click the body'' to enter inline edit mode (matches orga-app / priv-app behaviour); ''Ctrl-Enter'' to leave edit mode (handled by `rr-text-editor/leave-edit` toolbar shortcut). Fix: the popup ''Edit'' button no longer silently no-ops — `⛶ Edit` was rendered as text outside the `<$button>`'s body, so the click target was a 0-content button. Text moved inside the button. Per-note inline-edit state moved to `$:/state/rimir/knowledge-app/inline-edit/<noteTitle>` so multiple notes can be edited in different sessions without clobbering each other |
|0.1.2 |2026-04-30 |Edit a knowledge note from inside the app. Two modes: ''Inline'' toggles a body-only `$edit-text` with live save (no draft), exited via a Done button. ''Edit (popup)'' opens a full editor (title, fields, body) using TW's standard `$:/core/ui/EditTemplate` inside a navigator — same pattern as appify's view-edit overlay — with Save / Cancel actions that drive the draft via `tm-save-tiddler` / `tm-cancel-tiddler`. The pre-0.1.1 Edit button silently did nothing because there was no navigator in the appify widget tree to handle `tm-edit-tiddler`; both new modes work because they either avoid the message (inline) or wrap a navigator inline (popup) |
|0.1.1 |2026-04-30 |Knowledge ''areas'' (llm, it-security, health, gaming + user-creatable). Areas are tiddlers tagged `$:/tags/rimir/knowledge-app/area` with optional caption / icon / color metadata; the sidebar discovers areas as the union of registered + first-segment-of-existing-notes. New `area` channel between `section` and `topic`; topbar gets a second-row pill list with `+ Area` to register new ones at runtime. Quick-capture honours the active area (capture path becomes `knowledge/<area>/inbox/`, body opens with `\context knowledge/<area>`). Browse view filters by area + tier. Sidebar adapts: shows the area list when no area is selected, and the selected area's sub-topic tree when one is. Cross-area links keep working unchanged via namespace walk-up |
|0.1.0 |2026-04-30 |Initial release. Appify app under `knowledge/` namespace with Home, Browse, Note, Write, Search sections. Quick-capture; three-tier status (fleeting/developing/evergreen); backlinks panel via `ns-backlinks`; Write-tab maintenance views (orphans, stubs, dead-ends, broken refs); custom `_index` pseudo; starter `kn` mount; namespace feature flags enabled on install. Jasmine + Playwright test suites |
